{"title":"2020 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 7b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2020 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_7b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all pairs of angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accb77de5cd140f27f8c02226b444b0f5644bbe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x; y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/7740a1965d00b4a11335adefcb3fd4af01b10f51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^\\circ \\le x &lt; 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" />  and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f4b518f040f80c4230c745aee4c967a41b9e837.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^\\circ \\le y &lt; 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> that satisfy the following system of equations:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f5194eeb3caf4dbb818b3aeab614bcde4483479f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(\\sin x \\cos y) = \\frac{-3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"174\" height=\"38\" /><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b69cc51d0178f90818ec8e9c8a027f610a1a273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos y}) = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"125\" height=\"42\" /></center>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Logarithm_Rules.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Logarithm_Rules)\">Solution 1 (Logarithm Rules)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_7b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Logarithm Rules)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> degrees (inclusive of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8f3a072de64627a11a2df663e577eb43d60c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> must be either positive or zero. However, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8f3a072de64627a11a2df663e577eb43d60c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> is zero, then the product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8f3a072de64627a11a2df663e577eb43d60c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f1870419a299d737cd61066e3ffa1620c7ec2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982f1f896fb30b42065761ef5196f52f8204d22a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$log_2(\\sin x \\cos y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We can also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c942a316ee4efd35e46023dcf3256ef90e9814db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"11\" /> is positive because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982f1f896fb30b42065761ef5196f52f8204d22a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$log_2(\\sin x \\cos y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" /> would not be defined if the product was non-positive.\n</p><p>Thus, from the two equations, we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb2a75caba258b457869c74c0b0cd75b18f8544.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(\\sin x) + log_2(\\cos y) = \\frac{-3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"238\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b6c015a9efdd6ad214c26a37aa6a59fbba0f359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(\\sin x) - log_2(\\cos y) = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"224\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Adding these equations, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23f802677b9e137c5ab1adebf6f8088505dcba4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(\\sin x) + log_2(\\cos y) + log_2(\\sin x) - log_2(\\cos y) = \\frac{-3}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"480\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/403853c1616bf827cf9a3eb7e0b57c32da19ba31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2log_2(\\sin x) = \\frac{-3 + 1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"174\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/5/cc5f264261feb53447c6b47ebb292650712a4005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$log_2(\\sin^2 x) = \\frac{-2}{2} = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e78e949bc2e18ff0954f825ff2401febfb6c80ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 x = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/763b3b190414fe2dd454aac19b2f769518bbe351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x = \\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"107\" height=\"45\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8f3a072de64627a11a2df663e577eb43d60c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> was established to be positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689c81d34315ff9c5caf0f7c326d60e575a81c2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"93\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47ba626f81f48069ef19110d5bbcd27bad059f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"90\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>This means that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/6966e654dda59a2e2945653f1149938491c99bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e328afc726fa56c26ab4486cb108fdd5768c2b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 135^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8f3a072de64627a11a2df663e577eb43d60c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88eb239050e2aaac9f57007877ae5761e5ba1f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$log_2(\\sin x) + log_2(\\cos y) = \\frac{-3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"238\" height=\"38\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82ee57cf0fc29b65db18c241e8903c60c49cf1a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}) + log_2(\\cos y) = \\frac{-3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"231\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f4a11db20a09335027de1172828467e4b31a27d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2} + log_2(\\cos y) = \\frac{-3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"185\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a197274ce4c5c14a84931934322ae0f64dc1d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$log_2(\\cos y) = \\frac{-3}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} =  \\frac{-3 + 1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"253\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2138cf700a2f49cdded88c225bca15ecc0c1c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$log_2(\\cos y) = \\frac{-2}{2} = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/219f258d96e0bd4de20456f1186dfe720dd8399b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos y = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This would mean that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/a/54aeaaceee24c7e31f5e098bf6fee050406bf258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> from the constraints.\n</p><p>Using our values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, the pairs would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/6250310a1f36f43ef3f5cbfe4faeea5d79188a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(45^{\\circ}, 60^{\\circ})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"87\" height=\"32\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c623e43a274b42d6ce71ca733350630a14136d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(135^{\\circ}, 60^{\\circ})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"96\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012713\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 143/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7819/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.899      1 2020_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_7\n100.00%    5.899      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35905:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012713 and revision id 279686. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}